From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:35:12 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Port aurora-silicon/m1n1's merged change #46 (56c3e07e)

dart: map into the inherited tables of a locked display DART

aurora-silicon/m1n1 #46 (aurora-silicon/fix/locked-dart-inherited-tables),
merged as 56c3e07e, ported as its merge diff against the first parent.
It carries two commits by Ryan Murray:

  db5d56c7 dart: map into the inherited tables of a locked display DART
  f76d3180 dart: note where the display view's stream is bounded, and test it

Upstream's merge note: the root cause was confirmed on a panel-less M1
Pro (iBoot leaves the t6000 dart-dcp locked); M2 and Neo were not
booted. Nothing in this port has been booted.

#46 replaces dart_init_adt_display(), which omacom 7e00d548 (Chris
Kearney) introduced. aurora-wip had it through its merge of omacom
integration/aurora (#44). The function this tree carried is
byte-identical to the one #46 replaced (bc79acc, 56c3e07e^1).

Conflict resolution, src/dart.c and src/dart.h: the #35 port kept omacom's
dart_init_adt_display() before #35's dart_set_bypass_fdt(), while
aurora-wip has it after. So #46's removal hunk did not apply, and its
new function and dart_adt_locked() conflicted with an empty side. The
old copy (with its comment) is removed and #46's two functions are
placed after dart_set_bypass_fdt(), with the declarations in upstream's
order. dart.c then matches 56c3e07e except for
dart_walk_locked_t8110(), which gains a register-window size argument
only in a later aurora-wip commit outside this port set (9fb5d7a0,
"dart: bound the locked T8110 walk by the DART's register window").

#46's test renames (test_t8103_display_dart.py ->
test_display_dart_view.py, test_t8103_inherited_reservation.py ->
test_display_inherited_reservation.py) carried the #35 port's fixture
edit with them.

Build (RELEASE=1 CHAINLOADING=1, clang/lld 23.1.4): no new warnings.
Host tests, macOS: 290 passed. Failures are only the set that also fails
at bc79acc on this host.

Hardware tested on: NOT YET
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
